        <mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b&gt;Reading notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Higher count → lower ceiling → smaller drive amplitude. With no trips the count holds for ≈30 s, then decays.&lt;br&gt;• As drawn, U48 output also ties back to the R253/R254 junction (positive feedback; would latch if taken literally).&lt;br&gt;• U27B has no feedback part drawn, so as drawn it is a comparator (switches at BACK_OFF_COUNT ≈ 2-10 V). A proportional amplifier was probably intended.&lt;br&gt;• The µC only reads the count (PE3) and the clamped command (PE4); the back-off itself is all hardware. SuperFilter &quot;Back-off Count&quot; (LOOP screen) is this value." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="0" y="580" width="1450" height="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
